 {
  "content": [
   {
    "text": "I labelled 1 column for job 1, but the file is not really a one-column file. It is semicolon-delimited, and the platform read it as comma-delimited, so all nine fields arrived as one column.\n\nThe profile names that column `column_1`, and I labelled it `phi: true`, `role: other`. The contract's comma delimiter is the drift cause, so the contract writer should check the delimiter before writing column rules. The nine fields inside it should be labelled as follows:\n\n- `member_id`: identifier, PHI\n- `first_name`: name, PHI\n- `last_name`: name, PHI\n- `dob`: date, PHI\n- `sex`: code, not PHI\n- `plan_code`: code, not PHI\n- `coverage_start`: date, not PHI\n- `coverage_end`: date, not PHI\n- `patient_ref`: identifier, PHI",
    "type": "text"
   }
  ],
